<title>UK: ICI Plc calls egm to vote on ICI Australia sale.</title>
<headline>ICI Plc calls egm to vote on ICI Australia sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Chemical Industries Plc said on Tuesday it had called an extraordinary general meeting (EGM) for June 30 in London, seeking shareholder approval for the sale of its 62.4 percent stake in ICI Australia.</p>
<p>The group said in a statement it was actively pursuing the sale through a global equity offering with a view, depending on market conditions, to conduct the offering in July. Further details are to be announced shortly, it added.</p>
<p>The sale is part of the 3.0 billion stg divestment programme announced on May 7 when the chemical company also said it was buying Unilever Plc's speciality chemicals businesses.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
